Use two nested for loops over index positions, both built with range.
The outer loop tracks the current position i; start min_index at i.
The inner loop scans from i + 1 to the end and updates min_index when it finds a smaller value.
After the inner loop, swap: lst[i], lst[min_index] = lst[min_index], lst[i].
The function sorts the list in place, so it does not need a return statement.
